    static let centJSON = #"""
{"id":"fmm_synthetic_cent","feature_id":"fmf_synthetic","role":"assistant","text":"## Short answer\n\nThe cent never comes from the tax or the cart math themselves — it comes from `applyDiscount()` in `src/pricing.js`, which **truncates** percent discounts (`Math.floor`) instead of rounding, after bouncing the amount through floating‑point dollars. Any cart where a percent discount lands on a half‑cent gets shorted by one cent.\n\n## The path a total takes\n\n1. `Cart.total()` (`src/cart.js:36`)\n   ```js\n   const discounted = applyDiscounts(this.subtotal(), this.discounts);\n   return discounted + tax(discounted, this.region);\n   ```\n2. `applyDiscounts` folds the discounts in order (`src/pricing.js:17`).\n3. The percent branch (`src/pricing.js:5`) does:\n   ```js\n   const dollars = subtotalCents / 100;          // integer cents -> float dollars\n   const discounted = dollars * (1 - discount.value / 100);\n   return Math.floor(discounted * 100);          // truncate, not round\n   ```\n4. `tax()` then does `Math.round(cents * rate)` on that already‑truncated amount.\n\n## Why it's off by one\n\nConcrete case, already written up in `test/cart.test.js:17`:\n\n- Lamp = `1015` cents, 10% off.\n- Correct: `1015 * 0.90 = 913.5` cents → should round to **914**.\n- What the code does: `Math.floor(913.5) = ` **913**.\n\nSo the customer is charged a cent less (or, if you expect floor semantics elsewhere, the total disagrees with the receipt/ledger by a cent). The test `\"percent discount on awkward price\"` expects `914` and currently fails.\n\nThere's a secondary, sneakier contribution: `subtotalCents / 100` then `* 100` is a float round‑trip. `10.15 * 0.9 * 100` can evaluate to something like `913.4999999999999`, so even if you swapped `floor` → `round`, you're still one representation error away from a bad cent. The fix is to stay in integers.\n\n## Why it's inconsistent (the real smell)\n\nThree different rounding policies in one money path:\n\n| Place | Policy |\n|---|---|\n| `money.toCents` (`src/money.js:1`) | `Math.round` |\n| `tax` (`src/pricing.js:24`) | `Math.round` (half‑up) |\n| percent discount (`src/pricing.js:9`) | `Math.floor` |\n\nAnd `applyDiscounts` rounds/truncates **at every step**, so with two stacked percentages the result depends on discount order — that's the \"sometimes\" in \"sometimes off by a cent.\"\n\n## The related failure next to it\n\nThe `fixed` branch (`src/pricing.js:12`) has no floor at zero:\n\n```js\nreturn subtotalCents - discount.cents;   // 300 - 500 = -200\n```\n\n`test/cart.test.js:24` expects `0` and fails. That negative propagates into `tax()` (negative tax base) and then into `checkout()` (`src/checkout.js:9`), where `charge()` rejects `amountCents <= 0` (`src/payments.js:6`) — **after** the stock reservations were already made, so the reservations leak because nothing releases them on throw.\n\n## The fix\n\nInteger math + round, and clamp the fixed discount:\n\n```js\nif (discount.type === \"percent\") {\n  return Math.round((subtotalCents * (100 - discount.value)) / 100);\n}\nif (discount.type === \"fixed\") {\n  return Math.max(0, subtotalCents - discount.cents);\n}\n```\n\nThat makes `1015 @ 10%` → `(1015 * 90) / 100 = 913.5` → `914`, and `300 − 500` → `0`, matching both failing tests.\n\nWant me to apply this patch (and add the missing `checkout` reservation-release on charge failure)?","status":"done","created_at":"2026-09-26T12:00:00Z","visibility":"conversation","skim":{"status":"ready","format":"breath_tight","prompt_version":"skim-v2","segmenter_version":1,"skim_version":1,"document":{"version":1,"format":"breath_tight","status":"answer","statusLabel":"Answer","headline":[],"blocks":[{"kind":"say","tokens":[{"t":"text","v":"The cent comes from "},{"t":"code","v":"applyDiscount"},{"t":"text","v":" "},{"t":"anchor","id":"a1","label":[{"t":"text","v":"flooring 913.5 to 913"}],"refs":["s10","s11","s12"]},{"t":"text","v":" instead of rounding, plus "},{"t":"anchor","id":"a2","label":[{"t":"text","v":"mixed rounding policies"}],"refs":["s17"]},{"t":"text","v":" and a float round-trip; the "},{"t":"anchor","id":"a3","label":[{"t":"text","v":"fixed branch can also go negative"}],"refs":["s20","s21","s22"]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"kind":"heads_up","tokens":[{"t":"text","v":"fixed discounts over the subtotal go negative, leaking stock reservations on checkout."}]},{"kind":"ask","tokens":[{"t":"text","v":"Want me to apply the "},{"t":"anchor","id":"a4","label":[{"t":"text","v":"integer-math patch"}],"refs":["s25","s26"]},{"t":"text","v":"?"}]}],"drawers":[],"rest":{"refs":["s2","s4","s5","s6","s7","s9","s13","s14","s16","s18","s24","s27"]},"anchors":[{"id":"a1","label":"flooring 913.5 to 913","refs":["s10","s11","s12"],"where":"block 1","kind":"text"},{"id":"a2","label":"mixed rounding policies","refs":["s17"],"where":"block 1","kind":"table"},{"id":"a3","label":"fixed branch can also go negative","refs":["s20","s21","s22"],"where":"block 1","kind":"code"},{"id":"a4","label":"integer-math patch","refs":["s25","s26"],"where":"block 3","kind":"code"}],"stats":{"sourceWords":477,"skimWords":46,"budget":{"max":35,"target":30},"links":4,"coveredWords":171,"totalWords":445,"coverage":0.3842696629213483},"warnings":[{"level":"warn","code":"over_budget","message":"Skim is 46 words; budget was 35."}]},"segments":[{"id":"s1","n":1,"kind":"heading","startLine":1,"endLine":1,"start":0,"end":15,"words":3,"section":"s1","level":2},{"id":"s2","n":2,"kind":"paragraph","startLine":3,"endLine":3,"start":17,"end":346,"words":49,"section":"s1"},{"id":"s3","n":3,"kind":"heading","startLine":5,"endLine":5,"start":348,"end":373,"words":6,"section":"s3","level":2},{"id":"s4","n":4,"kind":"item","startLine":7,"endLine":11,"start":375,"end":551,"words":15,"section":"s3","ordered":true},{"id":"s5","n":5,"kind":"item","startLine":12,"endLine":12,"start":552,"end":623,"words":8,"section":"s3","ordered":true},{"id":"s6","n":6,"kind":"item","startLine":13,"endLine":18,"start